From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 11:12:03 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 111/111] wifi: mt7668: build it into the kernel, and on 6.12

The MT8516 Echos' Wi-Fi (ADR 0031), in Pinna's monolithic kernel:

- Kconfig MT7668_WLAN under the MediaTek wireless vendors. Built in, the
  driver takes its CFG_BUILT_IN_DRIVER path, which uses cfg80211's
  is_world_regdom() instead of a second definition of it.
- lidar-mainline ported the driver to 7.3. It keeps the 7.3 signatures;
  gl_cfg80211_compat.{c,h} give older kernels thin wrappers, chosen by
  LINUX_VERSION_CODE where the API changed:
  - 7.3: the core assigns the cookie of remain_on_channel and mgmt_tx;
    before, the driver returns one (a nonzero counter);
  - 7.1: the key and station ops, cfg80211_new_sta() and
    cfg80211_del_sta() take the wireless_dev; before, the net_device;
  - 6.17: set_wiphy_params, set_tx_power and get_tx_power take
    radio_idx (-1, all radios);
  - 6.16: timer_container_of() was from_timer();
  - 6.14: get_tx_power takes link_id.

Builds for arm64 with gcc 15; not yet run on an MT7668. The driver
requests its firmware when the SDIO function probes, which for a
built-in driver is before the root is mounted.
